    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.44,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "The OD plateaus at about 0.43–0.45 from 5 h onward. I tested whether this was reader saturation by diluting the 18 h aliquot. At 3x dilution the readings were 0.149 and 0.156 (mean 0.1525), which is 0.457 after correcting for dilution. At 10x dilution the mean was 0.039 (0.043 and 0.035), which is 0.39 after correcting. Both are at or slightly below the undiluted reading of 0.443. If the undiluted reads were compressed by saturation, the dilution-corrected values would exceed the undiluted reading, and they do not. The plateau therefore looks like real stationary phase, and biomass at the final hours matches the undiluted readings."
  },
